14.2 Minor modes
================

 -- Command: org-agents-mode
     Buffer-local minor mode, ‘Agents’ in the mode line.  Updates this
     buffer's agents before each save, with no prefilter, skipping
     agents whose scope has no bound, and restoring the buffer where the
     render changed nothing.  Refuses a buffer that is not an Org
     buffer.  See *note org-agents-mode::.

 -- Command: global-org-agents-mode
     Turns ‘org-agents-mode’ on in every Org buffer whose text matches
     ‘^[ \t]*:AGENT_QUERY:’.  See *note global-org-agents-mode::.

 -- Command: org-agents-faces-mode
     Buffer-local minor mode, ‘Attrs’ in the mode line.  Draws a
     headline in the face its resolved value for a declared attribute
     names, ahead of ‘org-level-N’ rather than instead of it.  Changes
     no bytes: one font-lock keyword, no text, no property, no overlay.
     Refuses a buffer that is not an Org buffer.  See *note Faces from
     attribute values::.

 -- Command: global-org-agents-faces-mode
     Turns ‘org-agents-faces-mode’ on in every Org buffer, and
     deliberately not only in those whose text mentions a property: a
     value arriving through a prototype is spelled nowhere.  See *note
     Faces in every Org buffer::.


