14.4 Agent properties
=====================

All ten are read from the entry's *own* drawer, with no inheritance of
any kind: not from an ancestor, not from a prototype, not from a
‘#+PROPERTY:’ line, not from ‘org-global-properties’.  A property line
written with nothing after it counts as absent.  Org itself reads the
value ‘nil’ as no value at all, so ‘:AGENT_VIEW: nil’ is an agent with
no view and takes the default.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_QUERY
     The agent's query: one line of Lisp, an org-ql S-expression
     extended with ‘$PROP’ references.  Required, and the property is
     what makes an entry an agent.  Unreadable text is refused by name;
     Lisp the gate does not admit is refused as ‘query not approved’.
     An Org property value is one line; see *note Putting a query in a
     property drawer::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_VIEW
     ‘children’ (the default), ‘list’ or ‘table’.  Any other value is
     refused rather than rendered.  See *note Choosing a view::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_SCOPE
     Which files the agent reads: ‘agenda’ (the default), ‘active’,
     ‘all’, a directory relative to ‘org-directory’, or a ‘read’-able
     list of file names (a value beginning with a parenthesis).  A
     directory that is not there is refused by name.  See *note
     Scopes::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_SORT
     ‘date’, ‘todo’, ‘priority’, ‘reverse’, or a list of those, which
     org-ql applies to the matched entries; or ‘(column N)’ /
     ‘(ts-column N)’, which order the rows of a table view and are
     refused in any other.  No sort when absent.  See *note Sorting and
     limiting::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_LIMIT
     A count, applied after the sort.  No limit when absent.  Anything
     that is not a count is refused rather than read as zero.  See *note
     Sorting and limiting::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_COLUMNS
     Whitespace-separated column names for a ‘table’ view.  ‘ITEM_BY_ID’
     is the link to the match, wherever in the list it appears; every
     other name is read as a property at the match.  Defaults to
     ‘ITEM_BY_ID’ alone.  A name nothing has set gives an empty cell.
     See *note The table view::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_FORMAT
     Whitespace-separated property names, shown after the link in the
     ‘children’ and ‘list’ views.  Read with no inheritance.  No suffix
     when absent.  See *note Formats::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_ACTION
     What to do to the entries the query matched, as a declarative
     sentence over the nine action verbs.  Read only by
     ‘org-agents-apply-actions’, from this entry's own drawer, never
     inherited, and never evaluated.  See *note Writing an action::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_MATCH
     Written by the package on a generated alias, never by hand.  ‘t’
     marks a heading as an alias this package may manage.  See *note The
     alias contract::.

 -- Agent Property: AGENT_MATCHED
     Written by the package after an update: the count and an inactive
     timestamp, as in ‘3 [2026-08-20 Thu 17:46]’.  For an agent carrying
     several blocks it is the first block's count, in buffer order.  See
     *note What writing AGENT_MATCHED costs::.


